### Your application

An application you make, for yourself or for a client, into which the software is built is different.  You may give it to other people, including customers, whether you built it with or without the `AUTOPILOT` conditional define, and whether it is your product or a test application you built with the test client of the software (`Autopilot.Client.pas`).  
Conditions:

  a. You distribute the application in compiled form - an executable, an installer, a mobile application package, or similar.
  b. What you distribute does not contain the source code of the software, its `.dcu` files, or any other form from which a person could recover the software as a unit reusable in their own projects.
  c. The main window of the application shows a visible link to the licensor's website, https://gabrielmoraru.com.  An application whose main window is never shown, or that has no graphical window (a console program, a service), shows the link in its documentation instead.

The licensor can waive condition c in writing, for a small fee.  To ask, contact the licensor through https://gabrielmoraru.com.
Apart from the link of condition c, you owe no credit, notice, or attribution inside your application.
A person who gets your application, from you or from someone you allowed, may use it and pass it on as you allow.  That person needs no license under these terms.

